        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> 1. Use `<C-V>` before typing each character\r\n\r\nWhy is this not an appropriate solution? This is the one I use, as this happens not that often.\r\n\r\nOf course, there is also a common way of disabling all 'mini.nvim' modules: [via `vim.g.minixxx_disable` and `vim.b.minixxx_disable`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/33e76b0c22465de03906ebd00c01b64a04e495b3/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L69) variables.\r\n\r\nYou can, for example, make this mapping to toggle autopairing:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<M-m>', '<Cmd>lua vim.g.minipairs_disable = not vim.g.minipairs_disable<CR>')\r\n```\r\n\r\nChoose mode, key, and global/buffer-local variable for you liking.\r\n\r\nDoes this solve your issue?",
