        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Edit: that is, I'd like to use `<c-v>`, but I'm not sure how to not mask the original `<c-v>` whilst doing so.\r\n\r\nThis is an almost perfect example of expression mappings. Those are first execute right hand side expression which should return an eventually needed value of right hand side. You can use it to first execute some of your code and then return `<C-v>`. Like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-v>', function()\r\n  vim.g.minipairs_disable = true\r\n  vim.cmd('au InsertLeave * ++once let g:minipairs_disable = v:false')\r\n  return '<C-v>'\r\nend, { silent = true, expr = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nYes, this code does have some Vimscript, but it has less nesting, so is better to me :)",
